; pi4V3dQpuAsm.pi4 - the QPU assembler's corpus, printed.
;
; DIAGNOSTIC. Does not ship. TOUCHES NO HARDWARE AT ALL except the
; UART it prints on - no V3D, no mailbox, no timer, no MMU.
;
; ======================================================================
;  WHAT THIS PROGRAM IS FOR
; ======================================================================
;
;  It assembles a fixed list of QPU instructions with
;  RaspberryPi4/Lib/v3dqpu.pi4 and prints each one as two 32-bit
;  halves. It checks nothing itself and it has no verdict.
;
;  THE VERDICT COMES FROM SOMEWHERE ELSE, AND THAT IS THE POINT.
;  tools/a64/a64_v3d_qpu_check.py runs this image in the A64 emulator,
;  reads these lines, assembles THE SAME LIST with py-videocore6 -
;  a complete independent implementation of this instruction set,
;  written by a third party from the same hardware - and compares all
;  sixty-four bits of every instruction.
;
;  Every other gate in this project compares a model this project
;  wrote against a document this project read. This one compares two
;  transcriptions that share no author, no language and no reasoning.
;
;  IT ALSO RUNS ON THE BOARD, and there is a small reason to. The A64
;  code generator is the thing under test everywhere else in this
;  tree; running the same corpus on silicon says the shifts and masks
;  the emulator interpreted are the shifts and masks the part
;  executes. It costs one image and thirty seconds.
;
; ======================================================================
;  THE LINE FORMAT, AND WHY IT IS THIS UGLY
; ======================================================================
;
;    I <index> <hi8> <lo8> <name>
;    R <index> <code> <name>
;
;  `I` is an instruction that packed; `R` is one the library REFUSED,
;  with the refusal code. The index is decimal and increments over
;  both kinds, so the gate can insist the two lists are the same
;  length and in the same order - a corpus that has silently drifted
;  apart at entry forty is worse than no corpus, because it will
;  still agree about the first thirty-nine.
;
;  THE NAME IS THE KEY AND IT IS CHECKED. The gate holds the same
;  names beside its py-videocore6 expressions and refuses if any name
;  is missing, extra or out of order. A gate whose needle matched a
;  label rather than the value beside it is a defect this project has
;  already had once (see a64_v3d_check.py's mutation notes), so the
;  gate parses the HEX and the NAME and demands both.
;
;  No columns, no padding, one space between fields. This is machine
;  output and a human reading it wants to diff it.
;
; ======================================================================
;  WHAT THE CORPUS COVERS
; ======================================================================
;
;  Section 1  the zero-source ADD operations, where BOTH mux fields
;             carry the operation's identity rather than an operand.
;             These are the ones a leftover register value silently
;             turns into a different instruction, so they are first.
;  Section 2  the one-source ADD operations, including the four
;             float-to-integer conversions and the six whose output
;             pack lives in the mux_b field.
;  Section 3  the two-source ADD operations, and the four
;             commutative float operations TWICE EACH with their
;             operands both ways round - which is the only thing that
;             tells FADD from FADDNF and FMIN from FMAX.
;  Section 4  the MUL half, every operation, reached by dual-issuing
;             against a NOP.
;  Section 5  dual issue and the register file: two register reads in
;             one instruction, which is the hardware's limit.
;  Section 6  small immediates from all three groups of the
;             forty-eight, including two of the sixteen that are
;             FLOAT BIT PATTERNS rather than integers.
;  Section 7  the signal field, twenty-one of its twenty-seven legal
;             values, including the six that put a WRITE ADDRESS in
;             the condition field instead of a condition.
;  Section 8  the condition field in nine of its eleven shapes.
;  Section 9  the branch form: all seven conditions, all four
;             destinations, the uniform-address extension, the
;             offset split, and the ONE BIT THE TWO IMPLEMENTATIONS
;             DISAGREE ABOUT.
;  Section 10 refusals. Twelve things the library must say no to.
;  Section 11 a real program built through the buffer and the hazard
;             checker, then dumped - which is the only section that
;             exercises V3dQpuEmit(), the memory writes and the
;             p37 restrictions.
;
;  SIX OPERATIONS THIS LIBRARY ENCODES ARE NOT IN THE CORPUS BECAUSE
;  THE ORACLE CANNOT CHECK THEM. py-videocore6's operation table
;  (assembler.py:740-809) has no fxcd, xcd, fycd, ycd, flafirst or
;  flnafirst, and no vadd or vsub. Putting them in the corpus would
;  mean the gate comparing this library against itself for those
;  eight lines, which is the exact thing this corpus exists to avoid.
;  They are transcribed in v3dqpu.pi4 with their table lines cited and
;  they are UNWITNESSED. Said here, and said again in the gate's
;  output, because an unwitnessed line inside a witnessed file is the
;  easiest kind of claim to over-read.
;
; ======================================================================

XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/v3dqpu.pi4"

#UART_DR = $FE201000
#UART_FR = $FE201018

; Where the section-11 program is built. Well clear of the image,
; which is linked at $400000, and of the stack top at $3000000.
#QPU_PROG_ADDR  = $700000
#QPU_PROG_BYTES = 4096

; The magic write addresses this file names, spelled out here rather
; than reached for from the library's constants so that a reader can
; see what a line does without a second file open.
#MW_R0    = 0
#MW_R1    = 1
#MW_R2    = 2
#MW_R3    = 3
#MW_R4    = 4
#MW_NULL  = 6
#MW_TMUD  = 11
#MW_TMUA  = 12
#MW_SYNCB = 18

Procedure PutC(c.i)
  Define f.i
  Repeat
    f = PeekN(#UART_FR)
  Until (f & 32) = 0
  PokeL(#UART_DR, c)
EndProcedure

Procedure PutS(*s)
  Define i.i
  Define c.i
  i = 0
  Repeat
    ; PeekA and not PeekB. PeekB names the SIGNED .b and sign-extends,
    ; so a byte above 127 would come back negative and this loop would
    ; run off the end.
    c = PeekA(*s + i)
    If c = 0 : Break : EndIf
    PutC(c)
    i = i + 1
  ForEver
EndProcedure

Procedure PutNl()
  PutC(13) : PutC(10)
EndProcedure

Procedure PutHex(v.i, digits.i)
  Define i.i
  Define n.i
  For i = digits - 1 To 0 Step -1
    n = (v >> (i * 4)) & $F
    If n < 10
      PutC(48 + n)
    Else
      PutC(55 + n)
    EndIf
  Next
EndProcedure

Procedure PutDec(v.i)
  Define d.i
  Define started.i
  Define digit.i
  If v < 0
    PutC(45)
    v = 0 - v
  EndIf
  If v = 0
    PutC(48)
    ProcedureReturn
  EndIf
  d = 1000000000000000000
  started = 0
  While d > 0
    digit = (v / d) % 10
    If digit <> 0 Or started = 1
      PutC(48 + digit)
      started = 1
    EndIf
    d = d / 10
  Wend
EndProcedure

; ======================================================================
;  THE EMITTERS THE CORPUS IS WRITTEN WITH
; ======================================================================
;
;  EVERY ONE OF THEM CALLS V3dQpuPack() AND NOT V3dQpuEmit().
;
;  That is deliberate and it is worth a paragraph. V3dQpuEmit() runs
;  the hazard checker, and the corpus IS NOT A PROGRAM - it is a
;  hundred and thirty unrelated instructions in a row, several of
;  which are thread switches three apart and branches next to
;  branches. Run through the hazard checker the corpus would be
;  refused at about entry ninety, and the refusal would be correct.
;
;  So the corpus tests the ENCODER and section 11 tests the EMITTER.
;  Conflating them would have meant either a corpus bent into a shape
;  the hazard rules allow - which is a corpus chosen by the checker
;  rather than by the encoding - or a hazard checker that had to be
;  turned off, which is a switch nobody should be able to reach.

Global idx.i = 0

Procedure Show(*name)
  Define r.i
  r = V3dQpuPack()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK
    PutS("R ")
    PutDec(idx)
    PutS(" ")
    PutDec(r)
  Else
    PutS("I ")
    PutDec(idx)
    PutS(" ")
    PutHex(V3dQpuHi(), 8)
    PutS(" ")
    PutHex(V3dQpuLo(), 8)
  EndIf
  PutS(" ")
  PutS(*name)
  PutNl()
  idx = idx + 1
EndProcedure

; A zero-source ADD. The muxes passed are junk on purpose: 7 and 7,
; which is the WORST possible leftover because mux 7 is the
; small-immediate slot. If the packer failed to substitute the fixed
; values these would all encode as VFLNB or worse, and the gate would
; see it immediately.
Procedure ShowA0(*name, op.i, waddr.i, magic.i)
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(op, waddr, magic, 7, 7)
  Show(*name)
EndProcedure

Procedure ShowA1(*name, op.i, waddr.i, magic.i, muxA.i)
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(op, waddr, magic, muxA, 7)
  Show(*name)
EndProcedure

Procedure ShowA2(*name, op.i, waddr.i, magic.i, muxA.i, muxB.i)
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(op, waddr, magic, muxA, muxB)
  Show(*name)
EndProcedure

Procedure ShowM2(*name, op.i, waddr.i, magic.i, muxA.i, muxB.i)
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuMul(op, waddr, magic, muxA, muxB)
  Show(*name)
EndProcedure

Procedure ShowM1(*name, op.i, waddr.i, magic.i, muxA.i)
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuMul(op, waddr, magic, muxA, 7)
  Show(*name)
EndProcedure

; A NOP carrying one signal, with the signal's destination.
Procedure ShowSig(*name, sigMask.i, sigWaddr.i, sigMagic.i)
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuSig(sigMask)
  V3dQpuSigAddr(sigWaddr, sigMagic)
  Show(*name)
EndProcedure

; A two-source ADD carrying flags.
Procedure ShowCond(*name, ac.i, mc.i, apf.i, mpf.i, auf.i, muf.i)
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_ADD, #MW_R0, 1, 1, 2)
  V3dQpuFlags(ac, mc, apf, mpf, auf, muf)
  Show(*name)
EndProcedure

; A two-source ADD and a two-source MUL in one instruction, carrying
; flags for both halves. The two-halves-both-conditional shapes are
; the ones the packing table is most likely to get wrong.
Procedure ShowCond2(*name, ac.i, mc.i, apf.i, mpf.i, auf.i, muf.i)
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_ADD, #MW_R0, 1, 1, 2)
  V3dQpuMul(#V3DQ_M_ADD, #MW_R3, 1, 0, 1)
  V3dQpuFlags(ac, mc, apf, mpf, auf, muf)
  Show(*name)
EndProcedure

Procedure ShowBranch(*name, cond.i, bdi.i, ub.i, bdu.i, setLink.i, offset.i, raddrA.i)
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuBranchSet(cond, #V3DQ_MSFIGN_NONE, bdi, ub, bdu, setLink, offset, raddrA)
  Show(*name)
EndProcedure

; An ADD with BOTH register-file read addresses set and an explicit
; magic bit. The VPM family needs this shape and the helpers above do
; not offer it: it puts a non-zero value in every field the family
; touches at once, which is what "a field is only pinned down by a
; value whose bits are not all zero" asks for.
Procedure ShowVpm(*name, op.i, waddr.i, magic.i, muxA.i, muxB.i, raddrA.i, raddrB.i)
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(op, waddr, magic, muxA, muxB)
  V3dQpuRaddr(raddrA, raddrB)
  Show(*name)
EndProcedure

; VFPACK with the two f32 input unpacks, which are the only thing that
; moves it between opcodes 53-55, 57-59 and 61-63.
Procedure ShowVfpackUnp(*name, waddr.i, magic.i, muxA.i, muxB.i, ua.i, ub.i)
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_VFPACK, waddr, magic, muxA, muxB)
  V3dQpuAddPacking(#V3DQ_PACK_NONE, ua, ub)
  Show(*name)
EndProcedure

; ======================================================================
;  SECTION 11's PROGRAM
; ======================================================================
;
;  IT IS pi4V3dCsd.pi4's SHADER, CHARACTER FOR CHARACTER, AND THE GATE
;  ENFORCES THAT. a64_v3d_qpu_check.py extracts this procedure and the
;  one in pi4V3dCsd.pi4, strips comments and whitespace, and requires
;  them to be identical - because the whole value of this section is
;  that the seventeen instructions the ORACLE checks here are the
;  seventeen instructions the BOARD runs there. Two copies that drifted
;  apart would leave the silicon running a program nothing had checked,
;  while this section went on passing.
;
;  Copied rather than shared because the alternative is a shader
;  builder in a library, and a shader for one diagnostic does not
;  belong in a library that everything else will include. The check
;  makes the copy safe; an unchecked copy would not be.
;
;    nop            sig = ldunifrf(rf0)   ; rf0 = the destination base
;    nop            sig = ldunifrf(rf1)   ; rf1 = the pattern seed
;    eidx  r0                             ; r0 = 0..15, the lane index
;    shl   r1, r0, 2                      ; r1 = lane * 4
;    add   r1, r1, rf0                    ; r1 = base + lane * 4
;    bor   r2, r0, rf1                    ; r2 = seed | lane
;    mov   tmud, r2                       ; the datum
;    mov   tmua, r1                       ; the address - THIS FIRES IT
;    tmuwt                                ; wait for it to land
;    ... the eight-instruction thread end
;
;  WHY THE DATUM IS SEED-OR-LANE AND NOT A CONSTANT. A constant
;  pattern proves the unit wrote; a per-lane value proves SIXTEEN
;  LANES each wrote, in the right places. "Wrote the same word
;  sixteen times" and "wrote sixteen different words" are
;  distinguishable answers and the second is the one worth having.
;
;  Returns #V3DQ_OK or the first refusal.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Procedure.i BuildShader()
  Define r.i

  r = V3dQpuProgramBegin(#QPU_PROG_ADDR, #QPU_PROG_BYTES)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK
    ProcedureReturn r
  EndIf

  ; The two uniforms, in the order the stream holds them. Each is a
  ; NOP carrying the LDUNIFRF signal, whose destination lives in the
  ; condition field - which is why an instruction with one of these
  ; may not also carry a condition.
  r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDUNIFRF, 0, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK
    ProcedureReturn r
  EndIf
  r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDUNIFRF, 1, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK
    ProcedureReturn r
  EndIf

  ; eidx r0. Zero-source: BOTH mux fields carry the operation's
  ; identity, so the values passed are ignored and substituted.
  r = V3dQpuAdd0(#V3DQ_A_EIDX, #MW_R0, 1)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK
    ProcedureReturn r
  EndIf

  ; shl r1, r0, 2. The 2 is small immediate index 2, on mux 7.
  r = V3dQpuAddImm(#V3DQ_A_SHL, #MW_R1, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, 0, 2)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK
    ProcedureReturn r
  EndIf

  ; add r1, r1, rf0. Mux 6 is raddr_a, which holds 0 - rf0.
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_ADD, #MW_R1, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1, #V3DQ_MUX_A)
  V3dQpuRaddr(0, 0)
  r = V3dQpuEmit()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK
    ProcedureReturn r
  EndIf

  ; bor r2, r0, rf1. The ADD half's OR; raddr_a is now 1 - rf1.
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_OR, #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_A)
  V3dQpuRaddr(1, 0)
  r = V3dQpuEmit()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK
    ProcedureReturn r
  EndIf

  ; mov tmud, r2 - the data register. Nothing happens yet.
  r = V3dQpuMov(#MW_TMUD, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R2, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK
    ProcedureReturn r
  EndIf

  ; mov tmua, r1 - WRITING THE ADDRESS REGISTER IS THE STORE.
  r = V3dQpuMov(#MW_TMUA, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1, 0)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK
    ProcedureReturn r
  EndIf

  ; tmuwt. Without it the thread can end with the store in flight.
  r = V3dQpuAdd0(#V3DQ_A_TMUWT, #MW_NULL, 1)
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK
    ProcedureReturn r
  EndIf

  r = V3dQpuThreadEnd()
  If r <> #V3DQ_OK
    ProcedureReturn r
  EndIf

  ProcedureReturn V3dQpuProgramEnd()
EndProcedure

; ======================================================================
Procedure Main()
  Define r.i
  Define i.i
  Define n.i

  PutNl()
  PutS("=== Pi 4 V3D stage 2 - the QPU assembler's corpus ===")
  PutNl()
  PutS("format: I index hi lo name | R index code name")
  PutNl()
  PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  1. ZERO-SOURCE ADD. Both muxes are the opcode.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ShowA0("nop",       #V3DQ_A_NOP,       #MW_NULL,  1)
  ShowA0("tidx",      #V3DQ_A_TIDX,      #MW_R0,    1)
  ShowA0("eidx",      #V3DQ_A_EIDX,      #MW_R1,    1)
  ShowA0("lr",        #V3DQ_A_LR,        #MW_R0,    1)
  ShowA0("vfla",      #V3DQ_A_VFLA,      #MW_R0,    1)
  ShowA0("vflna",     #V3DQ_A_VFLNA,     #MW_R0,    1)
  ShowA0("vflb",      #V3DQ_A_VFLB,      #MW_R0,    1)
  ShowA0("vflnb",     #V3DQ_A_VFLNB,     #MW_R0,    1)
  ShowA0("msf",       #V3DQ_A_MSF,       #MW_R0,    1)
  ShowA0("revf",      #V3DQ_A_REVF,      #MW_R0,    1)
  ShowA0("iid",       #V3DQ_A_IID,       #MW_R0,    1)
  ShowA0("sampid",    #V3DQ_A_SAMPID,    #MW_R0,    1)
  ShowA0("barrierid", #V3DQ_A_BARRIERID, #MW_SYNCB, 1)
  ShowA0("tmuwt",     #V3DQ_A_TMUWT,     #MW_NULL,  1)
  ShowA0("vpmwt",     #V3DQ_A_VPMWT,     #MW_R0,    1)

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  2. ONE-SOURCE ADD.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ShowA1("bnot",    #V3DQ_A_NOT,     #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA1("neg",     #V3DQ_A_NEG,     #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA1("flapush", #V3DQ_A_FLAPUSH, #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA1("flbpush", #V3DQ_A_FLBPUSH, #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA1("flpop",   #V3DQ_A_FLPOP,   #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA1("setmsf",  #V3DQ_A_SETMSF,  #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA1("setrevf", #V3DQ_A_SETREVF, #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA1("itof",    #V3DQ_A_ITOF,    #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA1("clz",     #V3DQ_A_CLZ,     #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA1("utof",    #V3DQ_A_UTOF,    #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA1("ftoin",   #V3DQ_A_FTOIN,   #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA1("ftoiz",   #V3DQ_A_FTOIZ,   #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA1("ftouz",   #V3DQ_A_FTOUZ,   #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA1("ftoc",    #V3DQ_A_FTOC,    #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA1("fround",  #V3DQ_A_FROUND,  #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA1("ftrunc",  #V3DQ_A_FTRUNC,  #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA1("ffloor",  #V3DQ_A_FFLOOR,  #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA1("fceil",   #V3DQ_A_FCEIL,   #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA1("fdx",     #V3DQ_A_FDX,     #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA1("fdy",     #V3DQ_A_FDY,     #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)

  ; The SFU operations. Note the destination: py-videocore6 spells
  ; these as recip(dst, src) and builds an ALU whose ADD operation is
  ; _op_recip, so the destination is an ordinary write address and
  ; NOT the magic RECIP register. Both spellings exist on this part -
  ; a write to magic waddr 19 also starts a reciprocal - and they
  ; encode differently. This corpus checks the operation form.
  ShowA1("recip",   #V3DQ_A_RECIP,   #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA1("rsqrt",   #V3DQ_A_RSQRT,   #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA1("exp",     #V3DQ_A_EXP,     #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA1("log",     #V3DQ_A_LOG,     #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA1("sin",     #V3DQ_A_SIN,     #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA1("rsqrt2",  #V3DQ_A_RSQRT2,  #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  3. TWO-SOURCE ADD.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ShowA2("add",  #V3DQ_A_ADD,  #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA2("sub",  #V3DQ_A_SUB,  #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA2("imin", #V3DQ_A_MIN,  #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA2("imax", #V3DQ_A_MAX,  #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA2("umin", #V3DQ_A_UMIN, #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA2("umax", #V3DQ_A_UMAX, #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA2("shl",  #V3DQ_A_SHL,  #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA2("shr",  #V3DQ_A_SHR,  #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA2("asr",  #V3DQ_A_ASR,  #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA2("ror",  #V3DQ_A_ROR,  #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA2("band", #V3DQ_A_AND,  #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA2("bor",  #V3DQ_A_OR,   #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA2("bxor", #V3DQ_A_XOR,  #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)

  ; THE FOUR COMMUTATIVE FLOAT OPERATIONS, EACH BOTH WAYS ROUND.
  ; FADD and FADDNF share opcodes 0-47 and FMIN and FMAX share
  ; 128-175; nothing but the operand order distinguishes them. If the
  ; packer's swap is missing, "fadd r0 r1" and "fadd r1 r0" come out
  ; identical and one of them is silently FADDNF - so these eight
  ; lines are the sharpest in the corpus.
  ShowA2("fadd01",   #V3DQ_A_FADD,   #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA2("fadd10",   #V3DQ_A_FADD,   #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0)
  ShowA2("faddnf01", #V3DQ_A_FADDNF, #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA2("faddnf10", #V3DQ_A_FADDNF, #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0)
  ShowA2("fmin01",   #V3DQ_A_FMIN,   #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA2("fmin10",   #V3DQ_A_FMIN,   #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0)
  ShowA2("fmax01",   #V3DQ_A_FMAX,   #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA2("fmax10",   #V3DQ_A_FMAX,   #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0)
  ShowA2("fsub",     #V3DQ_A_FSUB,   #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowA2("fcmp",     #V3DQ_A_FCMP,   #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)

  ; The float output packs and input unpacks, on FADD, which is the
  ; one arm that carries all three in the opcode's low six bits.
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_FADD, #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  V3dQpuAddPacking(#V3DQ_PACK_L, #V3DQ_UNPACK_NONE, #V3DQ_UNPACK_NONE)
  Show("fadd_packl")
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_FADD, #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  V3dQpuAddPacking(#V3DQ_PACK_H, #V3DQ_UNPACK_NONE, #V3DQ_UNPACK_NONE)
  Show("fadd_packh")
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_FADD, #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  V3dQpuAddPacking(#V3DQ_PACK_NONE, #V3DQ_UNPACK_ABS, #V3DQ_UNPACK_NONE)
  Show("fadd_absa")
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_FADD, #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  V3dQpuAddPacking(#V3DQ_PACK_NONE, #V3DQ_UNPACK_L, #V3DQ_UNPACK_H)
  Show("fadd_unplh")

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  4. THE MUL HALF. The ADD half stays a NOP with the default
  ;     destination, which is how py-videocore6 spells a
  ;     mul-only instruction.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ShowM2("mul_add",    #V3DQ_M_ADD,    #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowM2("mul_sub",    #V3DQ_M_SUB,    #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowM2("mul_umul24", #V3DQ_M_UMUL24, #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowM2("mul_smul24", #V3DQ_M_SMUL24, #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowM2("mul_multop", #V3DQ_M_MULTOP, #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowM2("mul_fmul",   #V3DQ_M_FMUL,   #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  ShowM1("mul_mov",    #V3DQ_M_MOV,    #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0)
  ShowM1("mul_movtmud", #V3DQ_M_MOV,   #MW_TMUD, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0)
  ShowM1("mul_fmov",   #V3DQ_M_FMOV,   #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0)

  ; FMUL's packs, which are added rather than ORed into the opcode -
  ; the one place in the encoding where that matters.
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuMul(#V3DQ_M_FMUL, #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  V3dQpuMulPacking(#V3DQ_PACK_L, #V3DQ_UNPACK_NONE, #V3DQ_UNPACK_NONE)
  Show("mul_fmul_packl")
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuMul(#V3DQ_M_FMUL, #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  V3dQpuMulPacking(#V3DQ_PACK_NONE, #V3DQ_UNPACK_ABS, #V3DQ_UNPACK_L)
  Show("mul_fmul_unp")
  ; FMOV's pack, which is SPLIT between the opcode and the mux.
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuMul(#V3DQ_M_FMOV, #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, 0)
  V3dQpuMulPacking(#V3DQ_PACK_H, #V3DQ_UNPACK_NONE, #V3DQ_UNPACK_NONE)
  Show("mul_fmov_packh")

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  5. DUAL ISSUE AND THE REGISTER FILE.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_ADD, #MW_R2, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  V3dQpuMul(#V3DQ_M_FMUL, #MW_R3, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_R1)
  Show("dual_add_fmul")

  ; band rf3, r0, rf1. One register-file read, on raddr_a, reached by
  ; mux 6; the destination is the register file too, so magic is 0.
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_AND, 3, 0, #V3DQ_MUX_R0, #V3DQ_MUX_A)
  V3dQpuRaddr(1, 0)
  Show("band_rf3_r0_rf1")

  ; add rf10, rf1, rf2. TWO register-file reads, which is the
  ; hardware's limit: raddr_a on mux 6 and raddr_b on mux 7.
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_ADD, 10, 0, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_B)
  V3dQpuRaddr(1, 2)
  Show("add_rf10_rf1_rf2")

  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_SHL, 5, 0, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_B)
  V3dQpuRaddr(5, 6)
  Show("shl_rf5_rf5_rf6")

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  6. SMALL IMMEDIATES, all three groups.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_ADD, #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1, #V3DQ_MUX_B)
  V3dQpuSmallImm(0)
  Show("add_imm0")
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_ADD, #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1, #V3DQ_MUX_B)
  V3dQpuSmallImm(15)
  Show("add_imm15")
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_ADD, #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1, #V3DQ_MUX_B)
  V3dQpuSmallImm(-1)
  Show("add_immm1")
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_ADD, #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1, #V3DQ_MUX_B)
  V3dQpuSmallImm(-16)
  Show("add_immm16")
  ; 1.0f. THE VALUE PASSED IS THE BIT PATTERN, not the number: this
  ; library has no float type and the table's last sixteen entries are
  ; f32 encodings.
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuMul(#V3DQ_M_FMUL, #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1, #V3DQ_MUX_B)
  V3dQpuSmallImm($3F800000)
  Show("fmul_imm1f")
  ; 2.0^-8, the bottom of the float group.
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuMul(#V3DQ_M_FMUL, #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1, #V3DQ_MUX_B)
  V3dQpuSmallImm($3B800000)
  Show("fmul_immtiny")
  ; mov rf5, 1 - py-videocore6 spells a move of an immediate as
  ; bor(dst, imm, imm), so BOTH muxes are 7 and the one immediate is
  ; read twice.
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_OR, 5, 0, #V3DQ_MUX_B, #V3DQ_MUX_B)
  V3dQpuSmallImm(1)
  Show("bor_rf5_imm1")

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  7. SIGNALS.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ShowSig("sig_thrsw",     #V3DQ_SIG_THRSW,     0, 0)
  ShowSig("sig_ldunif",    #V3DQ_SIG_LDUNIF,    0, 0)
  ShowSig("sig_ldunifa",   #V3DQ_SIG_LDUNIFA,   0, 0)
  ShowSig("sig_wrtmuc",    #V3DQ_SIG_WRTMUC,    0, 0)
  ShowSig("sig_ucb",       #V3DQ_SIG_UCB,       0, 0)
  ; The six that carry a WRITE ADDRESS in the condition field.
  ShowSig("sig_ldunifrf0",  #V3DQ_SIG_LDUNIFRF,  0,  0)
  ShowSig("sig_ldunifarf1", #V3DQ_SIG_LDUNIFARF, 1,  0)
  ShowSig("sig_ldtmu_r4",   #V3DQ_SIG_LDTMU,     4,  1)
  ShowSig("sig_ldvary_rf2", #V3DQ_SIG_LDVARY,    2,  0)
  ShowSig("sig_ldtlb_rf3",  #V3DQ_SIG_LDTLB,     3,  0)
  ShowSig("sig_ldtlbu_rf4", #V3DQ_SIG_LDTLBU,    4,  0)
  ; Combinations.
  ShowSig("sig_thrsw_ldunif",   #V3DQ_SIG_THRSW | #V3DQ_SIG_LDUNIF,   0, 0)
  ShowSig("sig_thrsw_ldunifrf", #V3DQ_SIG_THRSW | #V3DQ_SIG_LDUNIFRF, 7, 0)
  ShowSig("sig_thrsw_wrtmuc",   #V3DQ_SIG_THRSW | #V3DQ_SIG_WRTMUC,   0, 0)
  ShowSig("sig_ldtmu_ldunif",   #V3DQ_SIG_LDTMU | #V3DQ_SIG_LDUNIF,   4, 1)
  ShowSig("sig_thrsw_ldtmu",    #V3DQ_SIG_THRSW | #V3DQ_SIG_LDTMU,    4, 1)
  ShowSig("sig_ldvary_ldunif",  #V3DQ_SIG_LDVARY | #V3DQ_SIG_LDUNIF,  1, 0)
  ShowSig("sig_thrsw_ldvary",   #V3DQ_SIG_THRSW | #V3DQ_SIG_LDVARY,   1, 0)
  ShowSig("sig_ldvary_wrtmuc",  #V3DQ_SIG_LDVARY | #V3DQ_SIG_WRTMUC,  2, 0)

  ; A signal on a real instruction rather than a NOP.
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_ADD, #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1, #V3DQ_MUX_R2)
  V3dQpuSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDTMU)
  V3dQpuSigAddr(4, 1)
  Show("add_sig_ldtmu")

  ; SMIMM plus LDVARY is signal 14, and SMIMM plus LDTMU is 31 - the
  ; two rows of the table that pair the immediate with a load.
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_ADD, #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1, #V3DQ_MUX_B)
  V3dQpuSmallImm(15)
  V3dQpuSig(v3dq_sig | #V3DQ_SIG_LDVARY)
  V3dQpuSigAddr(1, 0)
  Show("add_imm_ldvary")
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_ADD, #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R1, #V3DQ_MUX_B)
  V3dQpuSmallImm(15)
  V3dQpuSig(v3dq_sig | #V3DQ_SIG_LDTMU)
  V3dQpuSigAddr(4, 1)
  Show("add_imm_ldtmu")

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  8. CONDITIONS AND FLAG UPDATES.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ShowCond("cond_apushz", #V3DQ_COND_NONE, #V3DQ_COND_NONE, #V3DQ_PF_PUSHZ, #V3DQ_PF_NONE, #V3DQ_UF_NONE, #V3DQ_UF_NONE)
  ShowCond("cond_apushn", #V3DQ_COND_NONE, #V3DQ_COND_NONE, #V3DQ_PF_PUSHN, #V3DQ_PF_NONE, #V3DQ_UF_NONE, #V3DQ_UF_NONE)
  ShowCond("cond_apushc", #V3DQ_COND_NONE, #V3DQ_COND_NONE, #V3DQ_PF_PUSHC, #V3DQ_PF_NONE, #V3DQ_UF_NONE, #V3DQ_UF_NONE)
  ShowCond("cond_ifa",    #V3DQ_COND_IFA,  #V3DQ_COND_NONE, #V3DQ_PF_NONE,  #V3DQ_PF_NONE, #V3DQ_UF_NONE, #V3DQ_UF_NONE)
  ShowCond("cond_ifnb",   #V3DQ_COND_IFNB, #V3DQ_COND_NONE, #V3DQ_PF_NONE,  #V3DQ_PF_NONE, #V3DQ_UF_NONE, #V3DQ_UF_NONE)
  ShowCond("cond_aandz",  #V3DQ_COND_NONE, #V3DQ_COND_NONE, #V3DQ_PF_NONE,  #V3DQ_PF_NONE, #V3DQ_UF_ANDZ, #V3DQ_UF_NONE)
  ShowCond("cond_anorc",  #V3DQ_COND_NONE, #V3DQ_COND_NONE, #V3DQ_PF_NONE,  #V3DQ_PF_NONE, #V3DQ_UF_NORC, #V3DQ_UF_NONE)

  ShowCond2("cond_mpushz", #V3DQ_COND_NONE, #V3DQ_COND_NONE, #V3DQ_PF_NONE, #V3DQ_PF_PUSHZ, #V3DQ_UF_NONE, #V3DQ_UF_NONE)
  ShowCond2("cond_mifb",   #V3DQ_COND_NONE, #V3DQ_COND_IFB,  #V3DQ_PF_NONE, #V3DQ_PF_NONE,  #V3DQ_UF_NONE, #V3DQ_UF_NONE)
  ShowCond2("cond_mandnz", #V3DQ_COND_NONE, #V3DQ_COND_NONE, #V3DQ_PF_NONE, #V3DQ_PF_NONE,  #V3DQ_UF_NONE, #V3DQ_UF_ANDNZ)
  ShowCond2("cond_ac_mpf", #V3DQ_COND_IFA,  #V3DQ_COND_NONE, #V3DQ_PF_NONE, #V3DQ_PF_PUSHZ, #V3DQ_UF_NONE, #V3DQ_UF_NONE)
  ShowCond2("cond_mc_apf", #V3DQ_COND_NONE, #V3DQ_COND_IFA,  #V3DQ_PF_PUSHZ, #V3DQ_PF_NONE, #V3DQ_UF_NONE, #V3DQ_UF_NONE)
  ShowCond2("cond_mc_ac",  #V3DQ_COND_IFA,  #V3DQ_COND_IFB,  #V3DQ_PF_NONE, #V3DQ_PF_NONE,  #V3DQ_UF_NONE, #V3DQ_UF_NONE)
  ShowCond2("cond_mc_auf", #V3DQ_COND_NONE, #V3DQ_COND_IFA,  #V3DQ_PF_NONE, #V3DQ_PF_NONE,  #V3DQ_UF_ANDZ, #V3DQ_UF_NONE)

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  9. BRANCHES.
  ;
  ;  BDU IS 1 IN ALL BUT ONE OF THESE, AND THAT IS NOT AN ODD CHOICE -
  ;  it is py-videocore6's constructor default (assembler.py:1075),
  ;  written unconditionally at :1121 whether or not UB is set. Mesa
  ;  writes BDU only when UB is set (qpu_pack.c:2485-2489). The two
  ;  DISAGREE about bits 17:15 of a branch with UB clear, and
  ;  "br_bdu0" below is the line that makes them say so out loud.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ShowBranch("br_always", #V3DQ_BR_ALWAYS, #V3DQ_BDEST_REL, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0)
  ShowBranch("br_a0",     #V3DQ_BR_A0,     #V3DQ_BDEST_REL, 0, 1, 0, $100, 0)
  ShowBranch("br_na0",    #V3DQ_BR_NA0,    #V3DQ_BDEST_REL, 0, 1, 0, $100, 0)
  ShowBranch("br_alla",   #V3DQ_BR_ALLA,   #V3DQ_BDEST_REL, 0, 1, 0, $100, 0)
  ShowBranch("br_anyna",  #V3DQ_BR_ANYNA,  #V3DQ_BDEST_REL, 0, 1, 0, $100, 0)
  ShowBranch("br_anya",   #V3DQ_BR_ANYA,   #V3DQ_BDEST_REL, 0, 1, 0, $100, 0)
  ShowBranch("br_allna",  #V3DQ_BR_ALLNA,  #V3DQ_BDEST_REL, 0, 1, 0, $100, 0)
  ShowBranch("br_abs",    #V3DQ_BR_ALWAYS, #V3DQ_BDEST_ABS, 0, 1, 0, $1000, 0)
  ShowBranch("br_link",   #V3DQ_BR_ALWAYS, #V3DQ_BDEST_LINK_REG, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0)
  ShowBranch("br_reg7",   #V3DQ_BR_ALWAYS, #V3DQ_BDEST_REGFILE,  0, 1, 0, 0, 7)
  ShowBranch("br_setlink", #V3DQ_BR_ALWAYS, #V3DQ_BDEST_REL, 0, 1, 1, $100, 0)
  ShowBranch("br_unifrel", #V3DQ_BR_ALWAYS, #V3DQ_BDEST_REL, 1, 1, 0, $100, 0)
  ShowBranch("br_unifabs", #V3DQ_BR_ALWAYS, #V3DQ_BDEST_REL, 1, 0, 0, $100, 0)
  ShowBranch("br_unifreg", #V3DQ_BR_ALWAYS, #V3DQ_BDEST_REL, 1, 3, 0, $100, 9)
  ; The offset split. $0ABCDEF8 exercises both halves and the
  ; three-bit hole at the bottom.
  ShowBranch("br_bigoff", #V3DQ_BR_ALWAYS, #V3DQ_BDEST_REL, 0, 1, 0, $0ABCDEF8, 0)
  ; THE DISAGREEMENT, on its own line.
  ShowBranch("br_bdu0",   #V3DQ_BR_ALWAYS, #V3DQ_BDEST_REL, 0, 0, 0, $100, 0)

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  9b. THE VPM FAMILY AND VFPACK, added at stage 4 because a vertex
  ;      shader cannot read an attribute or write a shaded vertex
  ;      without them and a fragment shader cannot write f16 colour
  ;      without VFPACK.
  ;
  ;      THE TWO HALVES OF THIS SECTION HAVE DIFFERENT EVIDENCE BEHIND
  ;      THEM AND THE GATE PRINTS THEM SEPARATELY.
  ;
  ;        - VFPACK and STVPMV/D/P are in py-videocore6's operation
  ;          table (assembler.py:744 and :804-806), so they are
  ;          ORACLE-CHECKED like everything above.
  ;        - THE SEVEN LDVPM OPERATIONS ARE NOT. py-videocore6 has no
  ;          ldvpm at all; in its tables opcode 188 is only reachable
  ;          as rsqrt/exp/log/sin/rsqrt2. Their expected words are
  ;          assembled by the GATE from the Mesa tables it parses,
  ;          which is a model against a model and is labelled as one.
  ;
  ;      THE STVPM ENTRIES ARE THE INTERESTING ONES. This file hands
  ;      the library waddr 0 every time and the library substitutes
  ;      0, 1 and 2 from the operation (qpu_pack.c:1578-1589) while
  ;      py-videocore6 is handed rf0, rf1 and rf2 explicitly. So the
  ;      OVERRIDE ITSELF is what the comparison tests: without it
  ;      stvpmd would encode waddr 0 and the oracle would say 1.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ShowVpm("vfpack",     #V3DQ_A_VFPACK, #MW_R0, 1, 1, 2, 0, 0)
  ShowVfpackUnp("vfpack_unp_lh", #MW_R0, 1, 1, 2, #V3DQ_UNPACK_L, #V3DQ_UNPACK_H)
  ShowVpm("vfpack_tlbu", #V3DQ_A_VFPACK, #V3DQ_WADDR_TLBU, 1, 1, 2, 0, 0)
  ShowVpm("stvpmv",     #V3DQ_A_STVPMV, 0, 0, 1, 2, 0, 0)
  ShowVpm("stvpmd",     #V3DQ_A_STVPMD, 0, 0, 1, 2, 0, 0)
  ShowVpm("stvpmp",     #V3DQ_A_STVPMP, 0, 0, 1, 2, 0, 0)
  ; THE OVERRIDE, AND THE MAGIC SUPPRESSION, ON ONE LINE. waddr 63 and
  ; magic 1 are both handed in and both must vanish: STVPMV has no
  ; destination operand at all (qpu_instr.c:479) and no_magic_write
  ; suppresses bit 44 (qpu_pack.c:1580, :1762). The expected word is
  ; identical to "stvpmv" above, which is the whole claim.
  ShowVpm("stvpmv_override", #V3DQ_A_STVPMV, 63, 1, 1, 2, 0, 0)

  ; The seven VPM loads. waddr 37 is 0b100101 so a shifted or narrowed
  ; destination field moves it; mux_a 6 reads raddr_a and mux_b 5 is
  ; DELIBERATE JUNK for the five forms whose mux_b carries the variant
  ; - if the packer failed to substitute, LDVPMV_IN would come out as
  ; LOG. raddr_a 27 and raddr_b 41 fill both six-bit read fields.
  ShowVpm("ldvpmv_in",   #V3DQ_A_LDVPMV_IN,  37, 0, 6, 5, 27, 41)
  ShowVpm("ldvpmv_out",  #V3DQ_A_LDVPMV_OUT, 37, 0, 6, 5, 27, 41)
  ShowVpm("ldvpmd_in",   #V3DQ_A_LDVPMD_IN,  37, 0, 6, 5, 27, 41)
  ShowVpm("ldvpmd_out",  #V3DQ_A_LDVPMD_OUT, 37, 0, 6, 5, 27, 41)
  ShowVpm("ldvpmp",      #V3DQ_A_LDVPMP,     37, 0, 6, 5, 27, 41)
  ; The gathered forms take TWO real sources, so mux_b 5 is an operand
  ; here and must survive.
  ShowVpm("ldvpmg_in",   #V3DQ_A_LDVPMG_IN,  37, 0, 6, 5, 27, 41)
  ShowVpm("ldvpmg_out",  #V3DQ_A_LDVPMG_OUT, 37, 0, 6, 5, 27, 41)

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  10. REFUSALS. Twelve things the library must say no to, entered
  ;      here rather than reasoned about, because a guard nobody has
  ;      seen refuse anything is a guard nobody knows is broken.
  ;
  ;      These print as `R index code name`. py-videocore6 has no
  ;      opinion about most of them, so the gate checks the CODE
  ;      against a list of its own rather than against the oracle -
  ;      and says so in its output, because that half is a model
  ;      agreeing with itself.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ; An operation this file does not encode. VFPACK AND STVPMV USED TO
  ; BE THESE TWO LINES and both are encoded since stage 4; the two
  ; operations named here are what is genuinely left of the 4.2 ADD
  ; table, so the refusal keeps testing a refusal rather than becoming
  ; a line that can no longer fail.
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_VFMIN, #MW_R0, 1, 0, 1)
  Show("ref_addop_vfmin")
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_VPMSETUP, #MW_R0, 1, 0, 1)
  Show("ref_addop_vpmsetup")
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_VDWWT, #MW_R0, 1, 0, 1)
  Show("ref_addop_vdwwt")
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuMul(#V3DQ_M_VFMUL, #MW_R0, 1, 0, 1)
  Show("ref_mulop_vfmul")
  ; A signal combination with no 4.2 encoding.
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuSig(#V3DQ_SIG_THRSW | #V3DQ_SIG_UCB)
  Show("ref_sig_thrsw_ucb")
  ; LDVPM, which is refused by name at the setter rather than at the
  ; table, so this one prints its code from V3dQpuSig()'s own path.
  V3dQpuReset()
  r = V3dQpuSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDVPM)
  PutS("R ")
  PutDec(idx)
  PutS(" ")
  PutDec(r)
  PutS(" ref_sig_ldvpm")
  PutNl()
  idx = idx + 1
  ; A condition on an instruction whose signal owns the field.
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDTMU)
  V3dQpuSigAddr(4, 1)
  V3dQpuFlags(#V3DQ_COND_IFA, #V3DQ_COND_NONE, #V3DQ_PF_NONE, #V3DQ_PF_NONE, #V3DQ_UF_NONE, #V3DQ_UF_NONE)
  Show("ref_flags_with_sig")
  ; A combination of conditions the table has no row for: an ADD
  ; condition and a MUL update.
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_ADD, #MW_R0, 1, 0, 1)
  V3dQpuMul(#V3DQ_M_ADD, #MW_R3, 1, 0, 1)
  V3dQpuFlags(#V3DQ_COND_IFA, #V3DQ_COND_NONE, #V3DQ_PF_NONE, #V3DQ_PF_NONE, #V3DQ_UF_NONE, #V3DQ_UF_ANDZ)
  Show("ref_flags_ac_muf")
  ; A pack on an operation that takes none.
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_ADD, #MW_R0, 1, 0, 1)
  V3dQpuAddPacking(#V3DQ_PACK_L, #V3DQ_UNPACK_NONE, #V3DQ_UNPACK_NONE)
  Show("ref_pack_on_add")
  ; ABS on a float-to-integer conversion, which has nowhere to put it.
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_FTOIZ, #MW_R0, 1, 1, 0)
  V3dQpuAddPacking(#V3DQ_PACK_NONE, #V3DQ_UNPACK_ABS, #V3DQ_UNPACK_NONE)
  Show("ref_abs_on_ftoiz")
  ; A value that is not one of the forty-eight small immediates.
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_ADD, #MW_R0, 1, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_B)
  r = V3dQpuSmallImm(17)
  PutS("R ")
  PutDec(idx)
  PutS(" ")
  PutDec(r)
  PutS(" ref_smallimm_17")
  PutNl()
  idx = idx + 1
  ; A small immediate asked for when raddr_b already holds a register.
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_ADD, #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_A, #V3DQ_MUX_B)
  V3dQpuRaddr(1, 2)
  r = V3dQpuSmallImm(3)
  PutS("R ")
  PutDec(idx)
  PutS(" ")
  PutDec(r)
  PutS(" ref_smimm_clash")
  PutNl()
  idx = idx + 1
  ; A write address outside the six-bit field.
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_ADD, 64, 0, 0, 1)
  Show("ref_waddr_64")
  ; A MAGIC DESTINATION ON A VPM LOAD. qpu_pack.c:1595 asserts
  ; !magic_write on this exact instruction; bit 44 is the IN/OUT
  ; selector for the seven LDVPM forms and not the magic flag, so a
  ; caller who asked for a magic destination asked for LDVPMV_OUT
  ; without knowing it. The ACCEPTED side of this guard is
  ; "ldvpmv_in" above, which passes magic 0 and encodes.
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_LDVPMV_IN, 5, 1, 6, 0)
  Show("ref_ldvpm_magic")
  ; ABS ON A VFPACK OPERAND. qpu_pack.c:1667-1670 returns false for it
  ; on either side, and the reason is visible in the opcode table: the
  ; five values an ABS operand would produce - 48-52, 56 and 60 - are
  ; exactly the ones the three VFPACK ranges skip. The ACCEPTED side
  ; is "vfpack_unp_lh", which uses L and H.
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_VFPACK, #MW_R0, 1, 1, 2)
  V3dQpuAddPacking(#V3DQ_PACK_NONE, #V3DQ_UNPACK_ABS, #V3DQ_UNPACK_NONE)
  Show("ref_vfpack_abs_a")
  ; AN OUTPUT PACK ON A VFPACK, WHICH THIS FILE IS STRICTER ABOUT THAN
  ; EITHER ORACLE. Mesa and py-videocore6 both ignore it; there is
  ; nowhere in the encoding to put one, so ignoring it produces an
  ; instruction that does something else. The ACCEPTED side is
  ; "vfpack" above, with PACK_NONE.
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_VFPACK, #MW_R0, 1, 1, 2)
  V3dQpuAddPacking(#V3DQ_PACK_L, #V3DQ_UNPACK_NONE, #V3DQ_UNPACK_NONE)
  Show("ref_vfpack_pack")

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  11. A REAL PROGRAM, THROUGH THE EMITTER.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  PutNl()
  r = BuildShader()
  PutS("P build ")
  PutDec(r)
  PutS(" hazard ")
  PutDec(V3dQpuHazardName())
  PutS(" count ")
  PutDec(V3dQpuCount())
  PutS(" bytes ")
  PutDec(V3dQpuProgramBytes())
  PutNl()

  If r = #V3DQ_OK
    n = V3dQpuProgramBytes() / 8
    i = 0
    While i < n
      PutS("S ")
      PutDec(i)
      PutS(" ")
      PutHex(PeekN(#QPU_PROG_ADDR + (i * 8) + 4), 8)
      PutS(" ")
      PutHex(PeekN(#QPU_PROG_ADDR + (i * 8)), 8)
      PutNl()
      i = i + 1
    Wend
  EndIf

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  12. THE HAZARD CHECKER, entered on purpose.
  ;
  ;      Each of these builds a fresh program in the same buffer and
  ;      drives it into one restriction. The line is
  ;      `H <name> <err> <hazard>`.
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  PutNl()

  ; Two TMU writes in one instruction - one from each half.
  V3dQpuProgramBegin(#QPU_PROG_ADDR, #QPU_PROG_BYTES)
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_ADD, #MW_TMUD, 1, 0, 1)
  V3dQpuMul(#V3DQ_M_ADD, #MW_TMUA, 1, 0, 1)
  r = V3dQpuEmit()
  PutS("H two_tmu ") : PutDec(r) : PutS(" ") : PutDec(V3dQpuHazardName()) : PutNl()

  ; An SFU write and then a read of r4 one instruction later.
  V3dQpuProgramBegin(#QPU_PROG_ADDR, #QPU_PROG_BYTES)
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_ADD, 19, 1, 0, 1)
  V3dQpuEmit()
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_ADD, #MW_R0, 1, #V3DQ_MUX_R4, 1)
  r = V3dQpuEmit()
  PutS("H sfu_r4 ") : PutDec(r) : PutS(" ") : PutDec(V3dQpuHazardName()) : PutNl()

  ; Two thread switches two apart.
  V3dQpuProgramBegin(#QPU_PROG_ADDR, #QPU_PROG_BYTES)
  V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_THRSW, 0, 0)
  V3dQpuNop()
  r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_THRSW, 0, 0)
  PutS("H thrsw_near ") : PutDec(r) : PutS(" ") : PutDec(V3dQpuHazardName()) : PutNl()

  ; A register-file write in a thread-end delay slot.
  V3dQpuProgramBegin(#QPU_PROG_ADDR, #QPU_PROG_BYTES)
  V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_THRSW, 0, 0)
  V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_THRSW, 0, 0)
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuAdd(#V3DQ_A_ADD, 5, 0, 0, 1)
  r = V3dQpuEmit()
  PutS("H rf_threnD ") : PutDec(r) : PutS(" ") : PutDec(V3dQpuHazardName()) : PutNl()

  ; LDUNIF immediately after LDVARY.
  V3dQpuProgramBegin(#QPU_PROG_ADDR, #QPU_PROG_BYTES)
  V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDVARY, 1, 0)
  r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_LDUNIF, 0, 0)
  PutS("H unif_vary ") : PutDec(r) : PutS(" ") : PutDec(V3dQpuHazardName()) : PutNl()

  ; A branch in a branch's delay slots.
  V3dQpuProgramBegin(#QPU_PROG_ADDR, #QPU_PROG_BYTES)
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuBranchSet(#V3DQ_BR_ALWAYS, #V3DQ_MSFIGN_NONE, #V3DQ_BDEST_REL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0)
  V3dQpuEmit()
  V3dQpuReset()
  V3dQpuBranchSet(#V3DQ_BR_ALWAYS, #V3DQ_MSFIGN_NONE, #V3DQ_BDEST_REL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0)
  r = V3dQpuEmit()
  PutS("H br_br ") : PutDec(r) : PutS(" ") : PutDec(V3dQpuHazardName()) : PutNl()

  ; A program with no thread end at all.
  V3dQpuProgramBegin(#QPU_PROG_ADDR, #QPU_PROG_BYTES)
  V3dQpuNop()
  r = V3dQpuProgramEnd()
  PutS("H no_threnD ") : PutDec(r) : PutS(" ") : PutDec(V3dQpuHazardName()) : PutNl()

  ; A buffer too small for the instruction being emitted.
  V3dQpuProgramBegin(#QPU_PROG_ADDR, 8)
  V3dQpuNop()
  r = V3dQpuNop()
  PutS("H buf_full ") : PutDec(r) : PutS(" ") : PutDec(V3dQpuHazardName()) : PutNl()

  ; A misaligned program buffer.
  r = V3dQpuProgramBegin(#QPU_PROG_ADDR + 4, #QPU_PROG_BYTES)
  PutS("H buf_align ") : PutDec(r) : PutS(" ") : PutDec(V3dQpuHazardName()) : PutNl()

  ; AND ONE THAT MUST BE ACCEPTED, at plus EIGHT.
  ;
  ; This line exists because a mutation run said so. The alignment
  ; refusal was mutated from `addr % 8` to `addr % 16` and SURVIVED:
  ; the only alignment case in this section was plus four, which is
  ; refused by both. A guard is only pinned down by a case on each
  ; side of it, and eight is the boundary the instruction word
  ; actually has.
  r = V3dQpuProgramBegin(#QPU_PROG_ADDR + 8, #QPU_PROG_BYTES)
  PutS("H buf_align8 ") : PutDec(r) : PutS(" ") : PutDec(V3dQpuHazardName()) : PutNl()

  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  ;  12b. THE SINGLE-SEGMENT PROGRAM, added at stage 4.
  ;
  ;  A vertex or coordinate shader that never switches threads is
  ;  SPAWNED ALREADY IN THE FINAL THREAD SECTION and its whole thread
  ;  end is one THRSW and three NOPs - no last-THRSW pair, because it
  ;  is already past that point. qpu_validate.c:430 encodes exactly
  ;  this as `.last_thrsw_found = !c->last_thrsw`.
  ;
  ;  THREE CASES, BECAUSE A GUARD NEEDS A CASE ON EACH SIDE. The same
  ;  four instructions must be ACCEPTED with singleSeg 1 and REFUSED
  ;  with singleSeg 0, and a second THRSW next to the first must be
  ;  refused as a duplicate last-THRSW marker (qpu_validate.c:314).
  ; ------------------------------------------------------------------
  V3dQpuProgramBeginSeg(#QPU_PROG_ADDR, #QPU_PROG_BYTES, 1)
  V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_THRSW, 0, 0)
  V3dQpuNop()
  V3dQpuNop()
  V3dQpuNop()
  r = V3dQpuProgramEnd()
  PutS("H singleseg_ok ") : PutDec(r) : PutS(" ") : PutDec(V3dQpuHazardName()) : PutNl()

  V3dQpuProgramBeginSeg(#QPU_PROG_ADDR, #QPU_PROG_BYTES, 0)
  V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_THRSW, 0, 0)
  V3dQpuNop()
  V3dQpuNop()
  V3dQpuNop()
  r = V3dQpuProgramEnd()
  PutS("H singleseg_off ") : PutDec(r) : PutS(" ") : PutDec(V3dQpuHazardName()) : PutNl()

  V3dQpuProgramBeginSeg(#QPU_PROG_ADDR, #QPU_PROG_BYTES, 1)
  V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_THRSW, 0, 0)
  r = V3dQpuNopSig(#V3DQ_SIG_THRSW, 0, 0)
  PutS("H singleseg_two ") : PutDec(r) : PutS(" ") : PutDec(V3dQpuHazardName()) : PutNl()

  PutNl()
  PutS("corpus entries ")
  PutDec(idx)
  PutNl()
  PutS("=== end ===")
  PutNl()

  ProcedureReturn idx
EndProcedure
